cient Greek ἀκτίς (aktís) 'ray, beam' and πτέρυξ (ptérux) 'wing, fins'), members of which are known as ray-finned fish or actinopterygians, is a class of bony fish that constitutes nearly 99% of the over 30,000 living species of fish. The vast majority of extant actinopterygian species are teleosts, and by species count they dominate the subphylum Vertebrata, comprising over 50% of all living vertebrates.","revisionId":1374607643,"title":"Actinopterygii","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Actinopterygii","wikidataId":"Q127282"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Crinifer","source":"Wikipedia"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Corythaixoides","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Corythaixoides A.Smith, 1833","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2475258},"ottId":842347,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Corythaixoides","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Crinifer is a genus of birds in the turaco family. They are restricted to Africa.","revisionId":1350938447,"title":"Crinifer","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crinifer","wikidataId":"Q570640"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Golden Lion Tamarin","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Leontopithecus rosalia","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Leontopithecus rosalia (Linnaeus, 1766)","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2436482},"ottId":921451,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Leontopithecus rosalia","synonyms":["Jacchus rosalia brasiliensis","Jacchus rosalia guyannensis","Leontocebus leoninus","Leontopithecus aurora","Leontopithecus marikina"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The golden lion tamarin (Leontopithecus rosalia; Portuguese: mico-leão-dourado [ˈmiku leˈɐ̃w do(w)ˈɾadu, - liˈɐ̃w -]), less commonly known as the golden lion marmoset, is a small New World monkey of the family Callitrichidae. Endemic to the Atlantic coastal forests of Brazil, the golden lion tamarin is an endangered species.","revisionId":1368879877,"title":"Golden lion tamarin","url":